ry  activity but there were suggestions that  there was also an inhibitory receptor  um we looked at hhla2 expression and  other v7s in normal kidney versus clear  cell renal carcinoma  and this analysis done by sam freeman  compares  um  in reddish  normal kidney and in blue  rcc  and what we saw very quickly  was that hhla2 was highly upregulated in  rcc pdl1 is just a little upregulated  pdl2 a little more  p7h3 upregulated  surprisingly b7h4 was down regulated  um  vista upregulated a little bit icos  little change  um there's lots of cd8 t cells uh in rcc  it's highly inflamed  so this said that hh la2 might be a good  target  and indeed we found hhla2 expressed in  multiple uh tumor types  high in renal pancreatic  adenocarcinoma the lung and colorectal  high in aml  um not in some other tumors  we made an immunohistochemistry antibody  uh as has zing zing zhang  and we found that some rcc didn't  express any hhla2 but that some  renal carcel  tumors  definitely expressed hhla2 on the  surface of the tumor cells  when we examined  with sabina signoreti and rupaulbot  of hhla2 and pdl1 expression in  rcc what we found  is that they weren't co-expressed  if they were co-expressed and each dot  here is  um  one  immunohistochemistry of one tumor  and what we see is we've plotted a pdl  one score or an hhla two score of each  tumor  if they were co-expressed  they would be out here in the upper  right quadrant but in contrast  the pdl1 scores  are all  along the left axis  there's not much shift to the right  indicating hhla2 expression  similarly the hhla2 if they express  highly  do not move up in pdl1 score  so they're not  co-expressed  in a rare tumor where we found that pdl1  and h802  were both expressed  they were expressed in different areas  this is  sequential sections by  immunohistochemistry  on the left is immune histochemistry of  hhla2  and you can see it's expressed in this  tissue down to the lower left  but  and in the next section we stain for 